Scaling changes the coefficient heights by an affine
function of $k$:
\[
    \log_{10}\|Q_{j,k}\|_2
    =\log_{10}a_k-\log_{10}a_j
      +(k-j)\log_{10}\gamma_j.
\]
Thus, it preserves the hull vertex indices and places
the dominant vertex at height zero. Points on the hull
segments adjacent to $j$ attain the decay bound;
the remaining points lie strictly below it.
